      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the **exact** value.\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the cosine double-angle identity:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(x\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(x\\right)=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the angle and evaluate the standard-angle cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{12}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
