      ":question/problem": "Without using a calculator, find the **exact** value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\cos^4\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad -2\\cos^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)\\sin^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&\\quad +\\sin^4\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)=\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $E$ denote the expression in the question. Recognize the expanded perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE &= \\left(\\cos^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)\\right)^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle identity:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2\\left(x\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(x\\right)=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute the angle and evaluate the standard-angle cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\cos^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(67.5^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(2\\cdot 67.5^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= \\cos\\left(135^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= -\\cos\\left(45^\\circ\\right) \\\\\n&= -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, square the value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE &= \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)^2 \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
